        <p>I’ve been called a “dream collaborator”, the one who goes “above and beyond”, “so deeply reliable” and many other things, but I tend to describe myself as an intermediary between people’s big ideas and their targeted, tangible results.</p>
        <p>Say you're launching a new film: I deal less with questions like “How do we become the most talked about film of the year”, and more with questions like “How do we reach the communities this film portrays, starting at the local level? And how do we engage them in ways that will raise the film's profile and, in turn, help us reach an even bigger audience?”.</p>
        <p>In the day to day, my fortes are information architecture, trust-based marketing, and design: UX, UI, graphic, and content.</p>
        <p>I’ve worked with freelancers, solo owners, boutique agencies, small businesses, and institutional departments, across education, nonprofit, B2B, and B2C.</p>
        <p>Feel like I could be the person you’re after?</p>
